# AI coding security awareness

Complements `cybersecurity.mdc` (full audit). Apply on **every** feature touching auth, API, DB, or deploy.

## REQ-067 — Blindspots checklist

| Risk | Before ship |
|------|-------------|
| SQL injection | Parameterized queries; no string concat SQL |
| XSS | Escape output; CSP where applicable |
| Secrets in repo | `.env` gitignored; scan with cybersecurity skill |
| Rate limiting | Public endpoints throttled |
| AuthZ gaps | Verify role checks on mutations |

## REQ-068 — Implementation quality

| Failure mode | Guard |
|--------------|-------|
| Hallucinated API | Verify against docs (`context7` MCP) or official fetch |
| Partial implementation | Acceptance criteria in handoff; no "TODO" in user-facing path |
| Type drift | Run typecheck/lint in squad-qa |
| Missing error paths | At least one failure case handled for external IO |

## Deploy / infra (REQ-066)

For deployment tasks: load `cybersecurity` skill + `docs/knowledge-base/SECURITY-AI-CODING.md`.  
Notion attachment Notes_260706 — principles inlined there; fetch via Notion MCP on demand.

## Veto

Do not commit `.env`, API keys, or OAuth JSON. `gitnexus_detect_changes()` before hub commits.
